{
  "api": "arsenal.piano.theory.scale_cases/v1",
  "about": "Scale corpus for arsenal/web/piano/scales.js (theory-nextgen-spec 2.4, TN0; frozen after TN0). NG6: the 11 prototype cases (design-engine 8.2), gate-closed cases give no canvas caption, roots spelled in the key, the vamps (D Dorian, A Dorian, A Aeolian), his Db loop none. Expectations are written by hand; the scale table is design-engine 8.1's, the gate table spec 2.4's.",
  "conventions": {
    "notes": "pitch names without octave; only the pitch class counts",
    "rank": "rankScales(chord pcs, weights, root pc, key): weights are 1 for chord notes and the given share for melody notes. expect.top is ranked[0].name on expect.root_name, spelled in the key (A7)",
    "sounded": "namingGate(scale, heard pcs, recent pcs): every character note of the scale (the gate table) is in the heard or the recent pitch classes; a scale with no gate entry never passes",
    "implied": "the scale's pitch classes that are neither heard (chord, melody) nor recent",
    "canvas": "the row may draw the scale caption: a key, the gate open, the chord diatonic in the key with a heard key tone outside its plain triad (a colour chord), and not the key's own Ionian over 1 or Aeolian over a minor tonic. Omitted where the spec leaves it open",
    "centre": "centreOf(chords, key): { root, mode } or null (the share values are not asserted)",
    "view": "createScaleView({ margin, holdMs }).update(ranked, t, same_window) at each step returns the scale expect names"
  },
